30,2,1,talk,Shizue,,"It seems our grants are quite short-term, which worries me. However, I noticed that community halls stayed open even when the roads were closed.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
31,2,1,talk,Jonathan,,"I've found that some of our residents have lost their bus links, making it very difficult for them to reach us. Our physical accessibility is currently lacking.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
32,2,1,talk,Rin,,"I found out that we tried digitizing photos before and it was a mess! But the outreach stops used to be super popular, even more than the main library!","{""words"":29,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
33,2,1,talk,Benjamin,,"Indeed, the funding structure is rather precarious. We have a habit of overspending on vehicle operations while letting equipment funds slide back into reserves.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
34,2,1,talk,Minako,,"I am concerned about our capacity. We have skilled volunteers for repairs, but no staff trained to supervise outside facilitators, and we've lost our tool certification technician.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
35,2,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, that sounds like a significant gap in our skills. We must be careful not to promise what we cannot safely manage.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
36,2,2,talk,Jonathan,,"@Rin, the popularity of those outreach stops combined with the loss of bus links suggests a strong need for us to go to the people.","{""words"":25,""mentions"":[""Rin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
37,2,2,talk,Rin,,Exactly! Why do we always stay in the building when people can't even get here? We should do something that moves!,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
38,2,2,talk,Benjamin,,"While a mobile service is tempting, the ledger suggests we struggle to fund the running costs of vehicles. We might be setting ourselves up for a deficit.","{""words"":27,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
39,2,2,talk,Minako,,"@Benjamin is right. Furthermore, if we start new programs requiring specialized supervision, we have no one on the payroll to handle it.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Benjamin""],""raw_differs"":false}"
40,2,3,talk,Shizue,,"If the community halls are accessible even in winter, perhaps a program that utilizes those existing spaces would be more stable than a vehicle.","{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
41,2,3,talk,Jonathan,,"That is a fair point, Shizue. But the remote catalogue use shows people want access at hours when our buildings are locked.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[""Shizue""],""raw_differs"":false}"
42,2,3,talk,Rin,,But the outreach stops worked! We just need to figure out how to make them stay this time instead of letting the funding lapse.,"{""words"":24,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
43,2,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The ""lapse"" is the key. The grant only covers the first year. Any expansion must be sustainable beyond that initial honeymoon period.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
44,2,3,talk,Minako,,I agree. We need a solution that doesn't rely on a single technician or a supervisor we don't actually have.,"{""words"":20,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
45,2,4,talk,Shizue,,Let us see the candidates and consider which one respects both our staff's limits and the community's needs.,"{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
46,2,4,talk,Jonathan,,I look forward to seeing if any of these options bridge the gap for those in the outer wards.,"{""words"":19,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
47,2,4,talk,Rin,,I hope there's something exciting that doesn't just end up as an unindexed pile of papers!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
48,2,4,talk,Benjamin,,Logic suggests we seek a balance between accessibility and fiscal durability.,"{""words"":11,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
49,2,4,talk,Minako,,I will be looking for the option that requires the least amount of unsupported specialized labor.,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
50,3,,status,Benjamin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":1,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
51,3,,status,Shizue,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":2,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
52,3,,status,Rin,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":3,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
53,3,,status,Jonathan,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":4,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
54,3,,status,Minako,,ALIVE,"{""seat"":5,""role"":""PARTICIPANT"",""alive"":true}"
55,3,1,talk,Shizue,,"Candidate A seems risky given the road closures and vehicle costs. Candidate C uses partner organizations, which might be more stable.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
56,3,1,talk,Jonathan,,"Candidate A directly addresses the bus link issue. However, Candidate C could also be hosted in those community halls that stay open.","{""words"":22,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
57,3,1,talk,Rin,,"A is the most fun! But I remember the digitizing fail, so D is a big no for me. C sounds like the evening groups that actually worked!","{""words"":28,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
58,3,1,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate A is a fiscal trap; the running costs will bleed us dry by year two. Candidate B requires a certified technician we no longer have.,"{""words"":26,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
59,3,1,talk,Minako,,"Candidate B is impossible without a certified technician. Candidate C requires supervising outside facilitators, which we also lack.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
60,3,2,talk,Shizue,,"@Minako, if Candidate C relies on partner organizations to coordinate, perhaps the burden on our staff is lower?","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[""Minako""],""raw_differs"":false}"
61,3,2,talk,Jonathan,,"If we choose C, we can place the circles in the outer wards, solving the accessibility problem without the cost of a vehicle.","{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
62,3,2,talk,Rin,,I like C! It's like the groups from six years ago that are still going. That means it actually works in real life!,"{""words"":23,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
63,3,2,talk,Benjamin,,Candidate C is the most logical. It leverages external facilitators and avoids the capital and operational pitfalls of A and B.,"{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
64,3,2,talk,Minako,,"If the partner organizations handle the primary coordination, it is the only viable option that doesn't create an immediate staffing crisis.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
65,3,3,talk,Shizue,,"I feel very comfortable with Candidate C. It is gentle, community-focused, and avoids the instability of the roads.","{""words"":18,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
66,3,3,talk,Jonathan,,It satisfies the need for outreach and accessibility while respecting the constraints of our current building hours.,"{""words"":17,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
67,3,3,talk,Rin,,I'm voting for C! It's the one that won't break or get lost in a basement!,"{""words"":16,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
68,3,3,talk,Benjamin,,"The financial structure of C is the least likely to collapse once the initial grant expires, provided the partners remain engaged.","{""words"":21,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
69,3,3,talk,Minako,,I concur. It is the most sustainable choice given our current roster of skills.,"{""words"":14,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
70,3,4,talk,Shizue,,It seems we have found a wonderful consensus.,"{""words"":8,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
71,3,4,talk,Jonathan,,Indeed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
72,3,4,talk,Rin,,Yay!,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
73,3,4,talk,Benjamin,,A rare moment of total alignment.,"{""words"":6,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
74,3,4,talk,Minako,,Agreed.,"{""words"":1,""mentions"":[],""raw_differs"":false}"
